WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.490
This is Hotel Lond Rose,
where Satoshi and Go are staying.

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:11.700
It looks like
they’re both out right now.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.500
Hmm?
Did they forget something?

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:21.420
Incoming call from Mr. Tsurugi!
Incoming call from Mr. Tsurugi!

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.500
Incoming call from Mr. Tsurugi!

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.190
Incoming call from Mr. Tsurugi!
Incoming call from—

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.400
Please enter your password!

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.240
Wrong password!

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.160
Wrong password!

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.830
Unlocked!

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.250
Opening album!

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.050
Should I look up information
about this Pokémon?!

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:40.560
Inteleon! Agent Pokémon! Water type!

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:46.600
The final evolution of Messon and Jimeleon!
Its signature move is Snipe Shot!

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:50.650
The water from its fingertips
is fired at Mach 3!

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.570
It picks out weak points
and hits them precisely!

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.120
Would you like to watch
a related video?!

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:05.210
This was back when Go’s Inteleon
was still just a Messon...

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:07.670
Oh, no!

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.550
Now! Delvil,
use Ember on them!

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.380
Poochyena! Shadow Ball!

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:17.550
What?!

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.360
Great going!

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.610
Messon’s really
looking up to Inteleon.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.420
Getting stronger will take time.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:04:00.010
So what do you think?
Would you like to train with me?

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:09.060
To become more like the Inteleon he admired,
Messon began training with Go.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:13.690
Even after evolving into Jimeleon,
he kept on training in silence and solitude.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.990
Then, one day, the Sakuragi Institute
had an intruder...

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:39.510
Something’s there!

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.430
A Kakuleon?!

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:47.770
It’ll get away with
the Institute’s priceless data!

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.810
Jimeleon tried to catch
the fleeing Kakuleon, but...

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.070
Jimeleon!

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.330
Are you okay, Jimeleon?!

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.920
Don’t worry! I’ll protect you!

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:32.100
You evolved...?

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.490
Now you’ve gone and made me...

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:47.990
...run for it, shi!

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.630
Snipe Shot!

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:02.130
Wh-Wh-Wha...?!

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:06.720
Wild! This is wild!

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.020
Shi?

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:11.850
All right!

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.770
He evolved into Inteleon,
as if answering Go’s call.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.530
He finally pulled off
the Snipe Shot he had admired.

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.530
And the case was solved.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:30.790
Incoming call from Mr. Tsurugi!
Incoming call from—

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.830
This is your regular check-in
from Project Mew.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:36.040
I’m only saying this once,
so listen care—

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:43.010
A message has arrived from Ms. Asahi!

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:45.260
Asahi here.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:47.680
I think Tsurugi will have
told you already,

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.850
but I’m sending you extra material
for the Mew search mission.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:53.140
Make sure to
commit it to memory.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:03.740
Project Mew.
Its goal is to search for Mew,

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:09.030
a mythical Pokémon that holds the genes of all Pokémon,
and is thought to be ancestor to all Pokémon.

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:15.120
A select few will conduct a search under the direction
of Project Leader Professor Hodaka.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:19.290
These are the five Chasers this time.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:25.090
Tsurugi, Shigeru, Tokio, Go,
and me, Asahi.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:29.680
Teamwork will be invaluable
in our search.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:33.560
In this extra material,
I’ll share data about the Chasers with you,

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:36.140
so you can better understand them.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.730
Go, Wulaosu!

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:40.940
First, Tsurugi.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:44.690
He passed the previous round
of Trial Missions with the highest score.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:50.120
He’s skilled at survival, and specializes
in fieldwork under harsh conditions.

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:53.040
He’s far from cooperative,

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:58.080
so relay any complaints to our mediator...
In other words, to me, Asahi.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:01.340
Next, Shigeru.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:05.840
He passed the current round
of Trial Missions with the highest score.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:11.260
Even if my goal seems impossible,
I’ll press on ahead without giving up.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:15.600
A researcher who travels
various regions to study Pokémon.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:20.270
He has a wide and deep range of knowledge
on a variety of fields.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:24.860
He carries a well-balanced style
which allows him to adapt to any situation.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.320
His Pokémon are also well-trained,

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:31.820
and as a trainer he has achieved excellent tournament placements.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.160
Next is Tokio.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:41.170
He’s a trainer pursuing Celebi, another Pokémon
considered a myth, similar to Mew.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.670
He’s well-versed in
Grass types and Psychic types.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:48.220
I thought that if I track down
every Psychic type, including Mew,

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:50.800
that might lead me
to Celebi, someday.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:55.600
His battle style specializes in support moves;
on defense and recovery.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:59.140
Mew’s capabilities are completely unknown.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:02.100
If a battle with Mew proves necessary,

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:05.150
we can count on him
to provide logistic support for the team.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:07.610
Lastly, Go.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:11.530
He travels various regions as a research fellow
for the Sakuragi Institute,

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.700
and has caught
over one hundred Pokémon.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:18.120
He’s one of the few trainers
to come into contact with Mew.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.830
I want to know
so much more about Pokémon.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.590
That’s why
I really want to see Mew again!

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:27.510
His investigative skills in finding
his target Pokémon...

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:30.930
...and his resourceful battle style
are his unique traits.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:36.140
We expect surprising situations
to be a constant in the search for Mew.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:41.440
We hope his analytical skills
and inventiveness will help us open a path to Mew.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:47.650
Those are the five Chasers
who will attempt the search for Mew.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:50.400
I’ll leave the strategy details
for another da—

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.570
Incoming call from Mr. Tsurugi!
Incom—

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:57.740
What did you hang up
out of nowhere for?

00:09:58.740 --> 00:09:59.450
Hey!

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.330
Are you listening?

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:04.500
Is that Sarunori?

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:07.960
Don’t tell me you’re the one
who hung up on—

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:28.900
Heyo!

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:32.240
A radio show for all you
potential future champions out there...

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.950
Afterschool Blaze Kick
starts now!

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:41.370
I’m your upperclassman, Narratah,
reciter of everyone’s dreams. Nice to meet you!

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:44.420
How’re you doing?
Enjoying your youth?

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:47.210
Got a Snipe Shot locked onto
winning the girl on your mind?

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:51.420
I bet you’re hesitating,
fearing she’ll Aqua Break your heart!

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:56.010
If you’re frozen stiff like Harden,
here’s a Blaze Kick to the rear!

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:56.010
There’s been a lot of new shows lately.

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:59.810
Our theme today is “childhood friends.”

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:03.520
Friends you’ve known
since childhood really are great.

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:08.690
First up is a message from
“The Port Town Flower Tender.”

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:13.740
“I’ve started listening to the radio lately,
thanks to my dad.

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:16.740
“If you read this out, it’ll be my first message read!”
Oh, thank you!

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:19.070
And thanks to your dad, too!

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:24.250
“My childhood friend
just loves Pokémon so much,

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.170
“and he’s so confident.

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:31.880
“He’s always going on saying
‘The future lies in my hands! I’ll catch Mew, for sure!’”

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:35.220
Ooh, big dreams are the best ones!

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:40.300
“He has a bit of a stubborn side,
and he even argues with his Pokémon.”

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.520
Huh...? Why does Hihidaruma
look so smug?

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:57.150
Hihidaruma provoked Hibunny
into trying to use Ember,

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.030
but it can’t really pull it off...

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:04.250
You should stop.

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:07.210
That’s enough.

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:14.300
Stop, Hibunny!

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:20.140
Your Lightning Speed and Double Kick
have gotten really strong.

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:22.640
It doesn’t matter if
you can’t use a Fire move.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:27.980
Looks like Hibunny
doesn’t agree with you.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.480
Well...

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:31.480
You can’t do
what you can’t do.

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:39.360
I told you, you don’t have...

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:42.910
Listen to me!

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:44.330
That’s just not good enough!

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:51.580
Ow!

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.090
Just accept that
there’s some things you <i>can’t</i> do!

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:58.720
Oh, what now?

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:00.800
Fine, then! Have it your way.

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.390
Hibunny!

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:10.690
What’s gotten into it?!

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:14.570
I tried so hard to bring out
Hibunny’s strength in battle.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:16.070
Really?

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:17.780
Yeah!

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:19.530
Oh, I see.

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:22.030
But that battle was...
How do I put it?

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.530
You and Hibunny
weren’t really one.

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:27.830
“One”?

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:33.500
Yeah! Like how when Pikachu and I battle,
it’s like we merge into one being!

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:37.090
And then it’s like our chest
starts boiling and blazing up...

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:41.220
and we go all <i>“Ba-Ba-Ba-Bang!”</i>

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:42.970
I have no idea what you mean...

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:47.850
Then you’ve gotta stick
with Hibunny until you <i>do</i> get it!

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:52.810
Hibunny!

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:55.810
That was...

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:59.280
Hey, wait, Hibunny!

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:04.110
Hibunny!

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:08.740
There might be a Fire move
you <i>can</i> use.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:12.250
Wanna try your Fire move?

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:18.000
Then stand in place
and use Lightning Speed!

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:21.340
Faster!

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.940
And then kick this!

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:44.700
This is our Ember!

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:52.500
“Putting the feelings of his Pokémon first,
they managed to pull off their very own Fire move!

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:56.540
“And with that move aiding him,
I hear he’s been on all these adventures.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:15:01.880
“This one time, he even told me
how he challenged a legendary Pokémon.”

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.260
Oh, you can’t believe that!

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:09.390
“I plan to keep cheering him on,
until the day he finds Mew!”

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:11.770
Thanks for your message!

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:16.650
Seeing their growth from up close...
Now <i>that’s</i> a perk of being childhood friends!

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:19.190
You <i>are</i> enjoying your youth!

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:21.480
Well then, onto the next message.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:27.070
Radio Name “A Timeless Bayleaf.”
Thanks again!

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:35.330
“Recently, I finally reunited with a friend
I lost contact with when I was young!

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:41.380
“Now, we’re allies working together
to reach the same goal, and he motivates me as my rival!”

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.710
It’s cold...

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:46.970
Get back!

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:58.810
Eerie Light!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.950
Absolute Zero?!

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:11.660
A one-hit KO move...

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.500
It’ll sweep you up
if you stick too close!

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:17.040
Try to battle from a distance!

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.250
Reflector!

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.710
Good choice!

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:29.260
Thanks, Tokio!

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:32.680
Don’t look away!
Focus on the battle!

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:33.640
Windie!

00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:36.270
Pyro Ball!

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:37.350
Aura Sphere!

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.230
Moonforce!

00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:45.820
Reflector!

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:00.420
Aceburn and Lucario,
grab onto Freezer!

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:02.130
Don’t just order them around!

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:03.500
Go, let’s do it.

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:09.220
Aceburn, grab onto Freezer!

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:10.720
You too, Lucario!

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:22.230
Flamethrower!

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:25.650
Blaze Kick!

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.280
Go, Lucario!

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.450
Heal Pulse!

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:46.710
Thank you, Tokio.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.090
Don’t let your guard down!

00:17:48.090 --> 00:17:50.010
Yeah, I know!

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:52.550
Satoshi,
let’s pile on the pressure!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:53.300
Yeah!

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:56.390
No! Freezer’s not some
easy little pushover!

00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:58.970
Aceburn!
Use Blaze Kick again!

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:00.770
Lucario, use Aura Sphere!

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:06.020
Sirknight, use Light Screen!

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:16.030
Windie! Flamethrower!

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:22.540
Aceburn!

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:26.170
Cheer up, Go.

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:28.300
There’ll be more missions.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:30.420
If you keep at it,
I’m sure you’ll make it!

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:31.720
Thanks.

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:34.720
Sometimes,
kindness can be a cruelty.

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:39.470
I cooperated with you today
because the mission was a Raid Battle,

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:43.060
but we Challengers don’t need to
play nice and pretend to be friends.

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:48.400
It’s fine! We can help
each other out as friends!

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:50.730
You’re as naïve as ever.

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:54.660
I agree with Mr. Tsurugi’s
strict mentality.

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:58.200
Without that strictness,
we’ll never encounter Mew.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:06.040
“I used to think that we should just all work together
as friends, since we were allies with the same goal,

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:09.500
“but watching him
and my other rivals...

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:13.670
“...has given me the chance
to learn about how others view things.”

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.030
Shigeru, let’s work together!

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:34.990
I’ve been waiting for you
to say that!

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:39.570
Use Pyro Ball on Regieleki!

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:42.450
Use Rocket Headbutt
on Regidrago!

00:19:57.430 --> 00:19:59.390
Kamex, use Rapid Spin!

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:01.300
Aceburn, get on Kamex!

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:08.060
Then use the Twister
to gain height!

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.610
Now!
Use Blaze Kick on Regieleki!

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.530
Charge in with Rapid Spin!

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:37.880
Come on, Monster Ball!

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:38.630
Monster Ball, go!

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:52.650
Go. Without your help,
I would never have caught it.

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:54.520
It’s teamwork
that gave us victory.

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:55.690
Shigeru...

00:20:56.070 --> 00:21:01.070
If you team up with someone unskilled
simply out of friendship, they’ll only let you down.

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:04.200
But even if you’re rivals
with someone...

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:07.080
...if your goals align,
you can still work together.

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:10.250
Stubbornly clinging to your pride
will only slow you down.

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:12.210
Acting alone
can prove fatal.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:17.090
That’s something I learned
from Mr. Tsurugi on a mission.

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:21.590
“We are walking
a long and steep path together.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:27.770
“Which is why I think we shouldn’t just be friends,
but also rivals pushing one another forward...

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:30.980
“...so that we can one day
reach our dreams, together!”

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:36.650
So you met long ago
and now you’re back together as rivals!

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:38.940
The flow of time is such a mystery!

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:44.570
Now, here’s a trendsetting song
that’s ahead of its time!

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:10.580
“The Cheerful Sarunori.”

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:15.830
“This is my first errand!
It will be easy!”

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:19.000
The plodding Sarunori.

00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:23.670
“Adventures are fun!
There are so many strange things!”

00:23:24.510 --> 00:23:26.680
The fearful Sarunori!

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:31.310
“Huh? Where am I?
I’m exhausted...”

00:23:32.600 --> 00:23:34.600
The weary Sarunori...

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:38.980
“I made a promise!
I have to see it through!”

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:42.610
The advancing Sarunori!

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:47.990
“Ah! There’s everyone!
I’m so close!”

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:51.370
The tearful Sarunori!

00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:56.160
“My errand went perfectly!
Didn’t I do great?!”

00:23:57.330 --> 00:23:59.420
The cheerful Sarunori!

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:04.130
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:24:04.130 --> 00:24:05.840
Go!

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:08.930
At last,
the finals are tomorrow!

00:24:09.390 --> 00:24:12.430
So today, let’s have a feast
and get some good rest!

00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:13.180
Huh?

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:15.310
That scone shop...

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:18.060
Do you remember, Aceburn?

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:20.360
This is where we met!

00:24:21.770 --> 00:24:23.690
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:24:23.690 --> 00:24:26.820
Go and Aceburn!
The Place It All Began!!
